  "title": "¡Qué Grande! --- The Same Word, Exclaiming",
  "drivablePrefix": 1,
  "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:131244a54a8cd9d3",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "ES-C64-que-grande",
      "sequence": 2475,
      "title": "¡Qué grande! — the same word, exclaiming",
      "headword": "¡Qué grande!",
      "romanization": "¡Qué grande!",
      "gloss": "how big! — the asking word doing a second job, keeping its accent because it is still the word carrying the force",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:9656b52009a60c90",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "¿Qué es esto? asks. And you have had the upside-down exclamation mark since the writing chapters, with nothing much to put between the pair."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here is what goes there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: qué in front of an adjective",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "¡Qué grande! — How big! ¡Qué bien! — How good! / Great!"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "No verb needed, nothing else needed. Qué plus an adjective or an adverb, between the two marks, and you have said something with force."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "¡Qué bien! in particular is worth having on the tip of your tongue. It is what Spanish says when English says nice! or great!, and it costs two words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Notice the accent. It is there in ¿qué? and it is here in ¡qué!, and by now you know why: that mark has never been about questions. It marks the word carrying the force of the sentence."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You saw the same thing when a reported question kept its accent inside a sentence with no question marks at all. Asking and exclaiming are two jobs, and the accent is the one thing they share."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plain que — no accent — is the joint you use for reporting and for relative clauses. It carries nothing, so it is marked with nothing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "¡Qué grande!, ¡Qué bien!",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *¡Qué grande!*, *¡Qué bien!*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
